    "https://www.nwciowa.edu/compass-center/alumni-resources": {
      "title": "Career resources for alumni",
      "description": "Alumni career resources  | Northwestern College in Iowa Skip Navigation MENU APPLY VISIT INQUIRE ESPAÑOL Search NWCIowa.edu Search Academics Challenge and support New learning and ideas will challenge you at Northwestern. But as part of our Christian academic community, you’ll also receive the support you need to make sense of it all. Academics @ NWC Academic programs Majors + programs Graduate & Professional Studies General education Degree requirements Meet standout Raiders Northwestern NEXT Academic excellence Opportunities Honors Program Internships Study abroad Resources Academic calendars Academic support + tutoring Bookstore Catalog Center for Innovation & Leadership Commencement Compass Center for Career & Calling Accessibility services Faculty directory Library Registrar Graduate + Online BELIEVE. ACHIEVE. Get an advanced degree with Northwestern College, online or on-campus. Our convenient and cost-competitive Graduate & Professional Studies programs are designed to fit your life. All Programs GRADUATE PROGRAMS Education Endorsements Master of Arts Clinical Mental Health Counseling Master of Arts School Counseling Master of Business Administration Master of Education Master of Science Nursing Education Physician Assistant MSPAS Teacher Leadership Certificate Teaching History Certificate OTHER ONLINE B.A. Early Childhood Coaching authorization Coaching endorsement Legal Interpreting Certificate Medical Interpreting Certificate ADMISSIONS Academic Calendar Apply New Student Steps Request Information Tuition + Financial Aid Resources Online Bookstore Resource Links Library Blog Podcast News Academic Catalogs CONTINUING ED Micro-credentials Upcoming events Admissions Explore. Belong. Our Christian college might be right for you. Learn how you’ll grow intellectually and spiritually. See what scholarships you qualify for. Visit us. Admissions @ NWC Connect Contact us Visit NWC Campus map Request information Quick facts Refer a student Virtual tour Why NWC? Information for Transfer students Hispanohablantes International students Military, veterans Graduate, online + adult learners Students w/ intellectual disabilities Parents + families Tuition + financial aid Tuition + financial aid Housing + food rates Scholarships Fees + other cost info Online bill payment Student consumer info Apply + enroll How to apply Admission requirements Enrollment deposit RED101 Days Raider Nation Orientation Campus life Focused and fun Your Northwestern education doesn’t stop when class is over. Some of the best lessons for life happen in your residence hall, on the court, during rehearsal, on a mission trip … Campus life @ NWC Community life Performing arts Campus dining Clubs + organizations Sports + fitness Community + belonging Orange City Residence life Residence halls Resident directors What to bring Support + resources Bridge Center Compass Center for Career & Calling Counseling + health Safety + security Student life staff Athletics Work hard. Play hard. At Northwestern, sports is training for life. The Raiders win, but the bigger victory is the lessons in character and commitment that last long after the season is over. Visit nwcraiders.com Men's sports Baseball Basketball Cheerleading Cross country Esports Football Golf Soccer Track + field Wrestling Women's sports Basketball Cheerleading Cross country Dance Esports Golf Soccer Softball Tennis Track + field Volleyball Wrestling Red Raiders Athletic band Camps Facilities Hall of Fame Photo gallery Raider Athletics Association Recruit info Athletics staff Webcast Fitness Center DeWitt Fitness Center Golf Practice Room Hours Fitness staff Faith Faith and courage A Northwestern education is for your head and your heart. Because the world needs people who are more than just smart. It needs brave Christians committed to making a difference. Faith @ NWC Campus ministry Staff Christian formation Calendar Watch + listen live Alumni Spread Red Stay connected to Northwestern by reading the Classic alumni magazine, attending alumni events, and encouraging smart Christian students to check out your alma mater. Alumni @ NWC Connect Classic magazine Shop NWC Compass Center for Career & Calling Meet our grads Update your information Events Calendar Raider Nation Celebration (Homecoming) Get involved Give to NWC Refer a student Distinguished alumni National Alumni Board Work at NWC Giving Mission Investment Giving to Northwestern is more than just making a donation. It’s an investment in Christian higher education and students who will make a difference in God’s world. Giving @ NWC Give now Credit card Support a cause Endowed gifts Raider Athletics Association Theatre Patrons Music Patrons Planned giving Beneficiary designations Charitable gift annuities Charitable lead trusts Charitable remainder trusts Endowed gifts Heritage Society Memorial gifts Real estate Wills and living trusts Resources Advancement staff Update your information About Faith and learning Since 1882, Northwestern has been delivering an excellent education within the context of community and a Christian worldview. About NWC Learn about NWC Academic excellence Community + belonging History + heritage Orange City, Iowa Quick facts Student consumer info Work for NWC Why NWC? Mission and values Our mission Christian identity statement Vision for Learning Vision for Diversity People Leadership President Greg Christy News + Events Information. Invitation. There’s always something going on at Northwestern. Stay current with Northwestern news. Come to campus for concerts, plays, art exhibits, Raider sports and more. News + events @ NWC News & media Press releases Videos Events Campus calendar Alumni events Athletic events Continuing education Music concerts Theatre productions Visual art exhibits Marketing & Communications NWC logos and photos MarCom and web staff MYNWC Your campus connection MyNWC is a Web-based system that allows you to access information about your financial aid, housing assignment, billing status, course schedule and academic records. MyNWC MyNWC Login Blackboard Login Career resources for alumni Most of the services of the Compass Center for Career & Calling are available free to alumni. You can: Receive personal career counseling Search job openings on Handshake Advertise job and internship openings, and recruit NWC students and graduates via Handshake YOU be the resource As a member of the more than 10,000-strong NWC alumni network, you are a valuable resource to our students. You can: Share your professional experiences and expertise as a mentor to students interested in careers like yours Help new graduates who’ve landed jobs in your area acclimate to their new community Learn more Explore Resources For students (MyNWC) For alumni For employers Staff Contact Compass Center for Career & Calling 712-707-7225 [email protected] Linked Home Academics Compass Center For alumni APPLY NOW VISIT CAMPUS NEWS & EVENTS CONTACT US PRIVACY POLICY Facebook Twitter Instagram Linked In YouTube More Social Media © 2026 Northwestern College. 101 7th Street SW • Orange City, Iowa 51041 • All rights reserved. LOADING …"
