for Transfer students Hispanohablantes International students Military, veterans Graduate, online + adult learners Students w/ intellectual disabilities Parents + families Tuition + financial aid Tuition + financial aid Housing + food rates Scholarships Fees + other cost info Online bill payment Student consumer info Apply + enroll How to apply Admission requirements Enrollment deposit RED101 Days Raider Nation Orientation Campus life Focused and fun Your Northwestern education doesn’t stop when class is over. Some of the best lessons for life happen in your residence hall, on the court, during rehearsal, on a mission trip … Campus life @ NWC Community life Performing arts Campus dining Clubs + organizations Sports + fitness Community + belonging Orange City Residence life Residence halls Resident directors What to bring Support + resources Bridge Center Compass Center for Career & Calling Counseling + health Safety + security Student life staff Athletics Work hard. Play hard. At Northwestern, sports is training for life. The Raiders win, but the bigger victory is the lessons in character and commitment that last long after the season is over. Visit nwcraiders.com Men's sports Baseball Basketball Cheerleading Cross country Esports Football Golf Soccer Track + field Wrestling Women's sports Basketball Cheerleading Cross country Dance Esports Golf Soccer Softball Tennis Track + field Volleyball Wrestling Red Raiders Athletic band Camps Facilities Hall of Fame Photo gallery Raider Athletics Association Recruit info Athletics staff Webcast Fitness Center DeWitt Fitness Center Golf Practice Room Hours Fitness staff Faith Faith and courage A Northwestern education is for your head and your heart. Because the world needs people who are more than just smart. It needs brave Christians committed to making a difference. Faith @ NWC Campus ministry Staff Christian formation Calendar Watch + listen live Alumni Spread Red Stay connected to Northwestern by reading the Classic alumni magazine, attending alumni events, and encouraging smart Christian students to check out your alma mater. Alumni @ NWC Connect Classic magazine Shop NWC Compass Center for Career & Calling Meet our grads Update your information Events Calendar Raider Nation Celebration (Homecoming) Get involved Give to NWC Refer a student Distinguished alumni National Alumni Board Work at NWC Giving Mission Investment Giving to Northwestern is more than just making a donation. It’s an investment in Christian higher education and students who will make a difference in God’s world. Giving @ NWC Give now Credit card Support a cause Endowed gifts Raider Athletics Association Theatre Patrons Music Patrons Planned giving Beneficiary designations Charitable gift annuities Charitable lead trusts Charitable remainder trusts Endowed gifts Heritage Society Memorial gifts Real estate Wills and living trusts Resources Advancement staff Update your information About Faith and learning Since 1882, Northwestern has been delivering an excellent education within the context of community and a Christian worldview. About NWC Learn about NWC Academic excellence Community + belonging History + heritage Orange City, Iowa Quick facts Student consumer info Work for NWC Why NWC? Mission and values Our mission Christian identity statement Vision for Learning Vision for Diversity People Leadership President Greg Christy News + Events Information. Invitation. There’s always something going on at Northwestern. Stay current with Northwestern news. Come to campus for concerts, plays, art exhibits, Raider sports and more. News + events @ NWC News & media Press releases Videos Events Campus calendar Alumni events Athletic events Continuing education Music concerts Theatre productions Visual art exhibits Marketing & Communications NWC logos and photos MarCom and web staff MYNWC Your campus connection MyNWC is a Web-based system that allows you to access information about your financial aid, housing assignment, billing status, course schedule and academic records. MyNWC MyNWC Login Blackboard Login Business-Economics Faculty Northwestern College invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track assistant professor of economics position beginning in August 2027. The teaching load is 24 credit hours per academic year, typically consisting of three courses per semester. In addition to teaching, the successful candidate will be expected to engage in scholarly activity and institutional service, including advising and recruiting students in the business and economics programs. The successful candidate will teach Principles of Finance Investments Advanced Corporate Finance and some of the following economics courses: Principles of Microeconomics Principles of Macroeconomics Intermediate Microeconomics Intermediate Macroeconomics Econometrics Money and Banking Behavioral Economics Managerial Economics There may be opportunities to teach other courses in the candidate’s areas of specialization. Required Qualifications: Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in economics or a closely related field to be considered for a tenure-track appointment; candidates who are ABD will also be considered. Applicants with a master's degree and substantial professional experience may be considered for appointment as an instructor or professor of practice. We seek faculty members who are committed to excellence in teaching, active scholarly engagement and the mission of the liberal arts as a vital expression of Christ's redemptive work in the world. Preferred Qualifications: Preferred candidates will demonstrate excellence in undergraduate teaching and maintain research interests that provide opportunities for meaningful student involvement. A strong commitment to collegiality, relationship-centered education, and student mentorship is highly valued. The business + economics department seeks a colleague who will contribute to our collaborative and supportive culture through service, shared purpose and a genuine commitment to helping students flourish academically, professionally and personally. Northwestern College seeks candidates with an authentic Christian faith who will embrace and live out our mission & values , including our Reformed, evangelical and ecumenical identity as stated in our Christian Identity Statement, Mission Statement, Vision for Learning and Vision for Diversity. We view these statements as complementary and draw from each in fulfilling our mission. Apply online below and send a current CV and a letter of interest to [email protected] . In your letter, please (1) summarize your teaching experience, (2) describe your scholarly trajectory, and (3) discuss how our Christian Identity Statement would inform and shape your teaching and scholarship. Incomplete applications won’t be considered. Application deadline is November 15, 2026 . Apply online To apply for this position, use the button below to start or resume your application. Apply now Explore Application process Application instructions Employment application Contact us FAQs Benefits Faculty Staff Handbooks Faculty Employee Resources Living in Orange City Insurance MRF Home About Work at NWC Current openings APPLY NOW VISIT CAMPUS NEWS & EVENTS CONTACT US PRIVACY POLICY Facebook Twitter Instagram Linked In YouTube More Social Media © 2026 Northwestern College. 101 7th Street SW • Orange City, Iowa 51041 • All rights reserved. LOADING …"
    },
