r Transfer students Hispanohablantes International students Military, veterans Graduate, online + adult learners Students w/ intellectual disabilities Parents + families Tuition + financial aid Tuition + financial aid Housing + food rates Scholarships Fees + other cost info Online bill payment Student consumer info Apply + enroll How to apply Admission requirements Enrollment deposit RED101 Days Raider Nation Orientation Campus life Focused and fun Your Northwestern education doesn’t stop when class is over. Some of the best lessons for life happen in your residence hall, on the court, during rehearsal, on a mission trip … Campus life @ NWC Community life Performing arts Campus dining Clubs + organizations Sports + fitness Community + belonging Orange City Residence life Residence halls Resident directors What to bring Support + resources Bridge Center Compass Center for Career & Calling Counseling + health Safety + security Student life staff Athletics Work hard. Play hard. At Northwestern, sports is training for life. The Raiders win, but the bigger victory is the lessons in character and commitment that last long after the season is over. Visit nwcraiders.com Men's sports Baseball Basketball Cheerleading Cross country Esports Football Golf Soccer Track + field Wrestling Women's sports Basketball Cheerleading Cross country Dance Esports Golf Soccer Softball Tennis Track + field Volleyball Wrestling Red Raiders Athletic band Camps Facilities Hall of Fame Photo gallery Raider Athletics Association Recruit info Athletics staff Webcast Fitness Center DeWitt Fitness Center Golf Practice Room Hours Fitness staff Faith Faith and courage A Northwestern education is for your head and your heart. Because the world needs people who are more than just smart. It needs brave Christians committed to making a difference. Faith @ NWC Campus ministry Staff Christian formation Calendar Watch + listen live Alumni Spread Red Stay connected to Northwestern by reading the Classic alumni magazine, attending alumni events, and encouraging smart Christian students to check out your alma mater. Alumni @ NWC Connect Classic magazine Shop NWC Compass Center for Career & Calling Meet our grads Update your information Events Calendar Raider Nation Celebration (Homecoming) Get involved Give to NWC Refer a student Distinguished alumni National Alumni Board Work at NWC Giving Mission Investment Giving to Northwestern is more than just making a donation. It’s an investment in Christian higher education and students who will make a difference in God’s world. Giving @ NWC Give now Credit card Support a cause Endowed gifts Raider Athletics Association Theatre Patrons Music Patrons Planned giving Beneficiary designations Charitable gift annuities Charitable lead trusts Charitable remainder trusts Endowed gifts Heritage Society Memorial gifts Real estate Wills and living trusts Resources Advancement staff Update your information About Faith and learning Since 1882, Northwestern has been delivering an excellent education within the context of community and a Christian worldview. About NWC Learn about NWC Academic excellence Community + belonging History + heritage Orange City, Iowa Quick facts Student consumer info Work for NWC Why NWC? Mission and values Our mission Christian identity statement Vision for Learning Vision for Diversity People Leadership President Greg Christy News + Events Information. Invitation. There’s always something going on at Northwestern. Stay current with Northwestern news. Come to campus for concerts, plays, art exhibits, Raider sports and more. News + events @ NWC News & media Press releases Videos Events Campus calendar Alumni events Athletic events Continuing education Music concerts Theatre productions Visual art exhibits Marketing & Communications NWC logos and photos MarCom and web staff MYNWC Your campus connection MyNWC is a Web-based system that allows you to access information about your financial aid, housing assignment, billing status, course schedule and academic records. MyNWC MyNWC Login Blackboard Login Assistant Softball Coach Northwestern College is seeking applicants for the position of assistant softball coach. Red Raider softball is seeking a candidate who can assist in leading a nationally contending program that won three consecutive GPAC titles from 2023-2025, and hosted back-to-back NAIA regionals in 2024-2025. Join the excellent Red Raider athletic department that claimed 5 GPAC titles this past year and sent 13 teams to the NAIA postseason. Responsibilities will include working with the head coach to administer and promote the softball program in a manner consistent with the mission and goals of Northwestern’s athletic department. The assistant coach will assist with practices, recruit athletes, and develop positive relationships with fellow coaches and athletes alike. This position will also involve responsibilities that may include teaching in the kinesiology curriculum or additional athletic department duties. The mission of Red Raider athletics is to “Honor Christ Through Excellence in Athletics.” The department core values include grit, gratitude, Christlike, competitive greatness, and focus. The Red Raider athletic vision seeks to Bring in student-athletes who desire to excel in all aspects of their life, Build them as individuals and athletes during their collegiate athlete experience, and Send them to championships on the competitive surface and ultimately out into the world as graduates of Northwestern College. A bachelor’s degree is required with master’s preferred, but all qualified candidates for the position will be considered. Applicants must possess excellent knowledge of the sport of softball and have experience as a softball coach at the college or high school level. Northwestern College seeks candidates with an authentic Christian faith who will embrace and live out our mission & values , including our Reformed, evangelical and ecumenical identity as stated in our Christian Identity Statement, Mission Statement, Vision for Learning and Vision for Diversity. We view these statements as complementary and draw from each in fulfilling our mission. Apply online below and send letter of application and resume to [email protected] . Apply online To apply for this position, use the button below to start or resume your application. Apply now Explore Application process Application instructions Employment application Contact us FAQs Benefits Faculty Staff Handbooks Faculty Employee Resources Living in Orange City Insurance MRF Home About Work at NWC Current openings APPLY NOW VISIT CAMPUS NEWS & EVENTS CONTACT US PRIVACY POLICY Facebook Twitter Instagram Linked In YouTube More Social Media © 2026 Northwestern College. 101 7th Street SW • Orange City, Iowa 51041 • All rights reserved. LOADING …"
